From 6e30e95bf02b7f4ff27a5b477ffc606f0d7b631d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mayor <git@hough.ink>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 12:14:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 62/73] witness: run orphaned-bead recovery on every patrol
 scan (feryn-ktm0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DetectOrphanedBeads — which scans FROM beads to catch hooked/in_progress
work assigned to polecats whose session is dead AND worktree directory is
gone — only ran at `gt up`. The witness patrol (`gt patrol scan`) ran only
DetectZombiePolecats, which scans FROM polecat directories and structurally
cannot see a bead whose polecat dir no longer exists.

Consequence: a daemon restart (or a reap) that removes a polecat's worktree
leaves its work bead stuck status=hooked assigned to a nonexistent polecat.
The convoy feeder then retries sling forever ("already hooked to
<polecat>") and skips, so the bead is never re-dispatched until the next
full `gt up`. Found live in the feryn self-healing stress run: 6 beads
(feryn-lorn/6jiw.4/qot6.2/07o3/pob9/cr3r) orphaned after the overnight
daemon restart, pipeline stalled.

Fix: add an "orphaned-bead recovery" phase to runPatrolScan that calls the
existing, tested DetectOrphanedBeads. Reuses resetAbandonedBead (on-main
guard + respawn circuit breaker + deacon re-dispatch mail). Surfaced in
JSON (orphans) and human output, and in the summary line. Runs after the
reap phase so it also clears beads left behind by this scan's own reaping.

Complements feryn-lxc6 (which fixed READING the hook under direct-tracking
when the polecat dir still exists); this covers the dir-gone case.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
